❌ Bad Way — Loading Everything into Memory

func StreamData(src io.Reader, dst io.Writer) error {
    data, err := io.ReadAll(src)  // Reads ENTIRE source into RAM
    if err != nil {
        return err
    }
    _, err = dst.Write(data)
    return err
}


✅ Good way to deal this 

func StreamData(src io.Reader, dst io.Writer) error {
    buf := make([]byte, 4096) // Reusable buffer
    _, err := io.CopyBuffer(dst, src, buf)
    return err
}

- Only 4KB in memory at any time regardless of file size
- Can stream a 10GB file without loading it all into RAM
- Buffer gets reused on each read/write cycle